==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm}} {{term|mawk|lang=enm}}, {{term|mauk|lang=enm}}, a contraction of {{term|mathek|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|non}} {{term|maðkr||maggot|lang=non}}, a diminutive of a base from {{proto|gem-pro|maþa-|worm|lang=en}} (Old English ''[[maþa]]''), from Indo-European ''*math-, moth-'' used in reference to insects and vermin.  Cognate with Danish ''[[madike]]'', Swedish ''[[mask]]'', archaic English ''[[maddock]]'' (modern ''[[maggot]]'').

